INT. COUNTY JAIL - ATTORNEY VISITING BOOTH - DAY

A narrow cinderblock booth split by a thick pane of scratched glass. A steel counter on either side, a black wall phone on each. Fluorescent hum. A clock on the wall behind the prisoner's side reads 2:14.

ATTORNEY ROSALINDA FAIRWEATHER-KIM, 40s, in a navy suit with a legal pad open on the counter, sits on a bolted stool. Across the glass sits her client, ERNESTINE VOSS-ADEBAYO, 60s, in an orange jumpsuit, hands folded, back straight as a rail. They each hold a receiver.

ROSALINDA
(into phone)
You look tired.

ERNESTINE (V.O.)
(over phone)
I'm sixty-three. I look tired.

ROSALINDA
Did they feed you?

ERNESTINE (V.O.)
(over phone)
A sandwich. I won't characterize it.

ROSALINDA
Ernestine, I need you to listen.

ERNESTINE (V.O.)
(over phone)
I'm listening.

ROSALINDA
The prosecutor offered a plea.

ERNESTINE (V.O.)
(over phone)
No.

ROSALINDA
You haven't heard it.

ERNESTINE (V.O.)
(over phone)
I've heard the word plea. That's enough.

ROSALINDA
Five years. Instead of fifteen.

ERNESTINE (V.O.)
(over phone)
I did not take the money.

ROSALINDA
I know.

ERNESTINE (V.O.)
(over phone)
Then why should I say I did?

ROSALINDA
Because a jury might say you did.

ERNESTINE (V.O.)
(over phone)
Let them.

ROSALINDA
They've got the ledger. They've got your signature on it.

ERNESTINE (V.O.)
(over phone)
My signature on a forged ledger.

ROSALINDA
We don't have proof of forged.

ERNESTINE (V.O.)
(over phone)
Then find it.

ROSALINDA
I have been looking for six months.

ERNESTINE (V.O.)
(over phone)
Look harder.

ROSALINDA
(a long breath)
Ernestine. I need you to understand what fifteen years means.

ERNESTINE (V.O.)
(over phone)
I'll be seventy-eight.

ROSALINDA
Yes.

ERNESTINE (V.O.)
(over phone)
And if I plead, I'll be sixty-eight, with a record, and everyone in the church will whisper.

ROSALINDA
That's one way to see it.

ERNESTINE (V.O.)
(over phone)
It is the way I see it.

She smooths the front of her jumpsuit, once, with the flat of her hand. Across the glass, the lawyer watches the gesture, then lowers her pen.

ROSALINDA
All right. Then we go to trial.

ERNESTINE (V.O.)
(over phone)
Thank you.

ROSALINDA
Don't thank me yet. I haven't won.

ERNESTINE (V.O.)
(over phone)
You haven't lost either.
